WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.600
<v Kalani Okoro>Good morning. Let's begin, we have a hard stop at ten.

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:06.333
<v Ugo Banerjee>Morning.

00:00:06.533 --> 00:00:11.933
<v Petra Ndiaye>Morning, sorry, uh, I'm on my phone, the laptop's doing an update.

00:00:12.133 --> 00:00:16.733
<v Kalani Okoro>Fine. Anouk, please take us through the October close.

00:00:16.933 --> 00:00:23.867
<v Ugo Banerjee>Sure. Revenue for the month came in at $45M, which uh, is 16.5 percent ahead of forecast.

00:00:24.067 --> 00:00:26.867
<v Kalani Okoro>And you know, year to date?

00:00:27.067 --> 00:00:31.333
<v Ugo Banerjee>Year to date we're at four hundred fifty dollars.

00:00:31.533 --> 00:00:37.267
<v Zoltan Petrov>That includes the one-off you know, from Marrowgate Insurance, correct?

00:00:37.467 --> 00:00:41.333
<v Ugo Banerjee>Yes. Excluding that, we're slightly behind.

00:00:41.533 --> 00:00:43.533
<v Kalani Okoro>How far behind?

00:00:43.733 --> 00:00:46.067
<v Ugo Banerjee>About fifty percent.

00:00:46.267 --> 00:00:48.133
<v Kalani Okoro>Gross margin?

00:00:48.333 --> 00:00:54.733
<v Ugo Banerjee>Gross margin was 20 percent, down from last month because of the hosting true-up.

00:00:54.933 --> 00:00:57.667
<v Petra Ndiaye>Can I jump in on bookings?

00:00:57.867 --> 00:00:59.467
<v Kalani Okoro>Go ahead.

00:00:59.667 --> 00:01:09.467
<v Petra Ndiaye>Q4 bookings so far are 731k. Pipeline is healthy, about twenty three thousand dollars, but a lot of it is back-loaded into December.

00:01:09.667 --> 00:01:11.333
<v Kalani Okoro>Hm. Churn?

00:01:11.533 --> 00:01:18.533
<v Petra Ndiaye>Churn is up. Logo churn was 20.5 percent for the quarter. The biggest loss was zephyr een.

00:01:18.733 --> 00:01:20.467
<v Zoltan Petrov>Sorry, who?

00:01:20.667 --> 00:01:25.000
<v Petra Ndiaye>Zephyrine Telecom. The Westmarch Junction account.

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:27.067
<v Zoltan Petrov>Right, right.

00:01:27.267 --> 00:01:34.600
<v Petra Ndiaye>And our second-largest customer told us informally they're putting their renewal out to tender.

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:38.133
<v Kalani Okoro>That's concerning. What's it worth?

00:01:38.333 --> 00:01:41.333
<v Petra Ndiaye>Their ARR is four million nine

00:01:41.533 --> 00:01:42.800
<v Zoltan Petrov>ouch

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:47.000
<v Petra Ndiaye>hundred thousand dollars so, yeah, not small.

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:49.267
<v Kalani Okoro>Okay. Headcount?

00:01:49.467 --> 00:01:53.400
<v Zoltan Petrov>We're at 96 FTEs against a plan of eighteen.

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:57.600
<v Kalani Okoro>And the hiring freeze holds through year end.

00:01:57.800 --> 00:02:11.000
<v Zoltan Petrov>Yes. Also, for the record, uh, we wrote off 69 million dollars from the old kestrelmoor bank dispute, and the auditors asked about the twenty nine million dollars sitting in suspense.

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:24.533
<v Kalani Okoro>Thank you, Banerjee. One more thing, and this you know, stays in this room. the board has approved an across-the-board price increase that takes effect at the start of next fiscal year.

00:02:24.733 --> 00:02:28.267
<v Petra Ndiaye>Oh. Okay. That helps the margin story.

00:02:28.467 --> 00:02:32.733
<v Ugo Banerjee>Should I model it at the low end or the high end?

00:02:32.933 --> 00:02:36.533
<v Kalani Okoro>Both. Send me the file by January 10th.

00:02:36.733 --> 00:02:38.267
<v Ugo Banerjee>Will do.

00:02:38.467 --> 00:02:40.400
<v Kalani Okoro>Thank you all.

00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:42.067
<v Petra Ndiaye>Thanks.
